<section id="requirements" class="docs-section">
<h2>@Localizer["Start with non-negotiable requirements"]</h2>
<p>@Localizer["Write down loads, operating temperature, chemical exposure, mating components, cosmetic faces, and expected life. Separate must-have requirements from preferences. A prototype for checking hand clearance needs different evidence from a replacement shaft carrying a rotating load. Identify which tests the prototype must represent before choosing its material or manufacturing route."]</p>
<p>@Localizer["Specify the material grade and condition when they matter. A printed polymer with a familiar family name is not automatically equivalent to an injection-molded grade; likewise, cast and wrought alloys should not be substituted by name alone. Compare the actual material data and test the characteristics that determine acceptance."]</p>
<p class="docs-source"><a href="https://www.protolabs.com/media/1022699/pl_digital_mfg_guide_2021.pdf">@Localizer["Source: Protolabs manufacturing process guide"]</a></p>
</section>
<section id="routes" class="docs-section">
<h2>@Localizer["Match geometry to a feasible route"]</h2>
<div class="docs-table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="@Localizer["Manufacturing route comparison"]"><table><thead><tr>
<th scope="col">@Localizer["Route"]</th>
<th scope="col">@Localizer["Useful starting point"]</th>
<th scope="col">@Localizer["Questions before selection"]</th>
</tr></thead><tbody>
<tr>
<th scope="row">@Localizer["CNC machining"]</th>
<td>@Localizer["Parts cut from stock; accessible precision interfaces and turned features."]</td>
<td>@Localizer["Can cutters reach the features? How many setups and how much stock removal are needed?"]</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<th scope="row">@Localizer["3D printing"]</th>
<td>@Localizer["Frequent design changes, complex shapes, and parts that benefit from additive geometry."]</td>
<td>@Localizer["Which technology, build direction, supports, finishing, and material properties are required?"]</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<th scope="row">@Localizer["Injection molding"]</th>
<td>@Localizer["Repeated polymer parts with a stable design and a justified tooling investment."]</td>
<td>@Localizer["Can the part eject? Review draft, wall transitions, gates, and tooling changes."]</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<th scope="row">@Localizer["Metal casting"]</th>
<td>@Localizer["Near-net shapes where the chosen casting method and alloy suit the application."]</td>
<td>@Localizer["Which casting method? Where are machining allowances, parting lines, and soundness requirements?"]</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<th scope="row">@Localizer["Sheet metal fabrication"]</th>
<td>@Localizer["Covers, brackets, and enclosures developed from sheet."]</td>
<td>@Localizer["Are bends accessible? Check bend radius, springback, fasteners, and weld distortion."]</td>
</tr>
</tbody></table></div>
<p class="docs-source"><a href="https://www.protolabs.com/en-gb/resources/blog/how-to-select-the-best-manufacturing-process-for-your-part/">@Localizer["Source: Protolabs process selection and product examples"]</a></p>
<p class="docs-source"><a href="https://www.xometry.com/resources/casting/die-casting/">@Localizer["Source: Xometry die casting explanation"]</a></p>
<p class="docs-source"><a href="https://www.protolabs.com/services/sheet-metal-fabrication/">@Localizer["Source: Protolabs sheet metal fabrication overview"]</a></p>
<p>@Localizer["Treat this table as a shortlist, not a purchase specification. Metal casting includes processes with different tooling, alloy, surface, and internal-quality implications. A route can also combine processes: cast a body and machine its bearing seats, or print a housing and machine selected interfaces. Ask which operations are included in the delivered price."]</p>

