<section id="economics" class="docs-section">
<h2>@Localizer["Compare total cost and repeat orders"]</h2>
<p>@Localizer["Request separate figures for engineering, fixtures or molds, first articles, unit production, secondary operations, inspection, packaging, and delivery. Compare the first order and expected repeat orders. Tool ownership, storage, maintenance, repair, and modification terms belong in the comparison because they affect the next revision as well as the first shipment."]</p>
<p>@Localizer["There is no universal quantity where one process becomes cheaper. Compare supplier quotations at realistic demand scenarios, including a lower-demand case. Keep the revision fixed, state batch sizes and delivery releases, and include rejected-part and rework responsibilities. A low unit price cannot compensate for buying inventory that becomes obsolete before assembly."]</p>
<p>@Localizer["Lead time includes more than machine time: material procurement, DFM approval, tooling, samples, qualification, finishing, and transport can control the schedule. Ask which event starts the quoted clock. For repeatability, agree the controlled characteristics and evidence needed across batches rather than assuming that automation alone proves consistency."]</p>
</section>
<section id="example" class="docs-section">
<h2>@Localizer["Example: a product changes process"]</h2>
<p>@Localizer["Protolabs reports that Epson used CNC machining for Moverio eyewear prototypes and later used injection molding for newer professional models. This is a documented example of process choice changing during product development; it does not establish a cost threshold, an interchangeable material, or a guaranteed schedule for another project."]</p>
<p>@Localizer["Apply that lesson to your own decision record: state what the current build must prove, which assumptions remain open, and what would trigger a process review. A change in geometry, annual demand, material certification, or inspection scope can justify a new comparison even when the previous batch worked."]</p>
<p class="docs-source"><a href="https://www.protolabs.com/en-gb/resources/blog/how-to-select-the-best-manufacturing-process-for-your-part/">@Localizer["Reference: Epson Moverio example in the Protolabs article"]</a></p>
</section>
<section id="handoff" class="docs-section">
<h2>@Localizer["Send a comparable quotation package"]</h2>
<p>@Localizer["Send matching CAD and drawing revisions, material and permitted alternatives, order quantity and forecast, critical interfaces, finish, inspection deliverables, and required delivery date. Invite suppliers to identify assumptions and exclusions. Record why the chosen route satisfies the requirements, and approve any design changes before releasing production files."]</p>
</section>
